An active counterclockwise rotation through a small angle $\epsilon$ sends $\psi(\theta)\longrightarrow\psi(\theta-\epsilon).$ Therefore $\begin{aligned}
\delta\psi(\theta)
&=\psi(\theta-\epsilon)-\psi(\theta)\\
&=-\epsilon\frac{d\psi}{d\theta}
+\mathcal O(\epsilon^2).\end{aligned}$

