Now calculate $=
[yp_z-zp_y,\;zp_x-xp_z].$ Most terms vanish. The two nonzero contributions are $\begin{aligned}
&=-i\hbar\,yp_x,\\
[zp_y,xp_z]&=i\hbar\,xp_y.\end{aligned}$ Therefore $\begin{aligned}
&=i\hbar\left(xp_y-yp_x\right)\\
&=i\hbar L_z.\end{aligned}$ Cycling the coordinate labels gives $\begin{aligned}
&=i\hbar L_z,\\
[L_y,L_z]&=i\hbar L_x,\\
[L_z,L_x]&=i\hbar L_y.\end{aligned}$

